#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186100680 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "20824866-0419-512a-b241-e3eb66b30194" :knowledge-point/title "Computing the Third-Degree Taylor Polynomial For a Function Given Some Derivatives"}] :question/id #uuid "6c57cb4e-244d-5058-91ef-9f74b15f2d35" :question/math-academy-id "e-7115" :question/problem "Let $f(x)$ be a function with $f(-1)=-1, f'(-1)=3, f''(-1)=-6$ and $f'''(-1)=6.$ What is the third-degree Taylor polynomial for $f(x)$ about $x=-1?$" :question/worked-solution "The third-degree Taylor polynomial of $f(x)$ about $x=-1$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{P}_{3}(x) & =f(-1)+{f}^{′}(-1)(x+1)+\\frac{{f}^{″}(-1)}{2!}(x+1)^{2}+\\frac{{f}^{‴}(-1)}{3!}(x+1)^{3} \\\\  & =f(-1)+{f}^{′}(-1)(x+1)+\\frac{{f}^{″}(-1)}{2}(x+1)^{2}+\\frac{{f}^{‴}(-1)}{6}(x+1)^{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe have been given the following set of values: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(-1) & =-1 \\\\ {f}^{′}(-1) & =3 \\\\ {f}^{″}(-1) & =-6 \\\\ {f}^{‴}(-1) & =6.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting the given values into our Taylor polynomial, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{P}_{3}(x) & =-1+3(x+1)+\\frac{(-6)}{2}(x+1)^{2}+\\frac{6}{6}(x+1)^{3} \\\\  & =-1+3(x+1)-3(x+1)^{2}+(x+1)^{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186100691 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "f9ea3dac-cf0a-5d05-8d77-7280ce9b5a94" :knowledge-point/title "Computing the Third-Degree Taylor Polynomial For a Given Function About a Given Point"}] :question/id #uuid "66991fe4-9891-5308-87cf-cd38a3bad4a4" :question/math-academy-id "e-741" :question/problem "Find the third-degree Taylor polynomial of $f(x) = \\ln(1+x)$ about $x=0.$" :question/worked-solution "To find the third-degree Taylor polynomial about $x=0,$ we plug $a=0$ into the general formula to give\n\n$$\nP_3(x) = f(0) + f'(0)(x-0) + \\dfrac{1}{2!}f''(0)(x-0)^2 + \\dfrac{1}{3!}f'''(0)(x-0)^3.\n$$\n\nWe need to compute $f(0),$ $f'(0),$ $f''(0),$ and $f'''(0),$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x) & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡(1+x) & ⟹ &  & f(0) & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡(1+0)=0 \\\\ {f}^{′}(x) & =(1+x)^{-1} & ⟹ &  & {f}^{′}(0) & =(1+0)^{-1}=1 \\\\ {f}^{″}(x) & =-(1+x)^{-2} & ⟹ &  & {f}^{″}(0) & =-(1+0)^{-2}=-1 \\\\ {f}^{(3)}(x) & =2(1+x)^{-3} & ⟹ &  & {f}^{‴}(0) & =2(1+0)^{-3}=2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we plug the results for $f(0),$ $f'(0),$ $f''(0),$ and $f'''(0)$ into our third-degree Taylor polynomial. This gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{P}_{3}(x) & =0+(1)(x-0)+\\frac{1}{2!}(-1)(x-0)^{2}+\\frac{1}{3!}(2)(x-0)^{3} \\\\  & =x-\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2}+\\frac{{x}^{3}}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186100692 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "5dc0250e-2aa9-5439-b567-93a59fa1c364" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Coefficient of a Term In the Third-Degree Taylor Polynomial of a Given Function"}] :question/id #uuid "33ce1593-08bc-539a-a7e0-c2805361d26e" :question/math-academy-id "e-742" :question/problem "What is the coefficient of $(x-1)^3$ in the third-degree Taylor polynomial of $f(x) = e^{-2x}?$" :question/worked-solution "The coefficient of $(x-1)^3$ is $\\dfrac{1}{3!}f^{(3)}(1).$ Let's compute the necessary derivatives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x) & ={e}^{-2x} \\\\ {f}^{′}(x) & =-2{e}^{-2x} \\\\ {f}^{″}(x) & =4{e}^{-2x} \\\\ {f}^{(3)}(x) & =-8{e}^{-2x}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{1}{3!}f^{(3)}(1) =\\dfrac{1}{6} \\left( -8e^{-2} \\right) = -\\dfrac{4}{3e^2}.\n$$\n\nSo the coefficient of $(x-1)^3$ is $-\\dfrac{4}{3e^2}.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186340391 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "f9ea3dac-cf0a-5d05-8d77-7280ce9b5a94" :knowledge-point/title "Computing the Third-Degree Taylor Polynomial For a Given Function About a Given Point"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4d5f2a9c-51b9-539f-8c6e-ea1a085f1ceb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x+\\frac{{x}^{3}}{2}-\\frac{{x}^{5}}{6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340393} {:answer/id #uuid "46b04293-c25f-59e0-ab1f-a7bedcc3b909" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1-x+\\frac{{x}^{3}}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340394} {:answer/id #uuid "0cf1e140-3a61-5f1f-8474-573dd7ff2134" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x+\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2}+\\frac{{x}^{3}}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340395} {:answer/id #uuid "b74a8e50-2478-5ef1-85ba-f9354727c79a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1-x+\\frac{{x}^{3}}{6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340396} {:answer/id #uuid "f6b6fcfa-66e0-54c2-bbdc-5c5072eac42c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1+\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2}+\\frac{{x}^{3}}{6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340397}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "46b04293-c25f-59e0-ab1f-a7bedcc3b909" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1-x+\\frac{{x}^{3}}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340394} :answer-field/id #uuid "d8bc7550-2675-595b-b9dc-de2d38777602" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340392}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "0115977e-e552-5c81-a528-e4c41764a6e8" :question/math-academy-id "q-12380" :question/problem "The third-degree Taylor polynomial of $f(x)={e}^{-x}\\operatorname{cos}⁡x$ about $x=0$ is" :question/worked-solution "To find the third-degree Taylor polynomial about $x=0,$ we plug $a=0$ into the general formula to give\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{P}_{3}(x) & =f(0)+{f}^{′}(0)x+{f}^{″}(0)\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2!}+{f}^{‴}(0)\\frac{{x}^{3}}{3!} \\\\  & =f(0)+{f}^{′}(0)x+{f}^{″}(0)\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2}+{f}^{‴}(0)\\frac{{x}^{3}}{6}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe need to compute $f(0),$ ${f}^{′}(0),$ ${f}^{″}(0),$ and ${f}^{‴}(0),$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x) & ={e}^{-x}\\operatorname{cos}⁡x & ⟹ &  & f(0) & ={e}^{-0}\\operatorname{cos}⁡0=1 \\\\ {f}^{′}(x) & =-{e}^{-x}\\operatorname{cos}⁡x-{e}^{-x}\\operatorname{sin}⁡x & ⟹ &  & {f}^{′}(0) & =-{e}^{-0}\\operatorname{cos}⁡0-{e}^{0}\\operatorname{sin}⁡0=-1 \\\\ {f}^{″}(x) & =2{e}^{-x}\\operatorname{sin}⁡x & ⟹ &  & {f}^{″}(0) & =2{e}^{-0}\\operatorname{sin}⁡0=0 \\\\ {f}^{‴}(x) & =-2{e}^{-x}\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+2{e}^{-x}\\operatorname{cos}⁡x & ⟹ &  & {f}^{‴}(0) & =-2{e}^{-0}\\operatorname{sin}⁡0+2{e}^{-0}\\operatorname{cos}⁡0=2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we plug the results for $f(0),$ ${f}^{′}(0),$ ${f}^{″}(0),$ and ${f}^{‴}(0)$ into our third-degree Taylor polynomial. This gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{P}_{3}(x) & =1+(-1)\\cdot x+0\\cdot \\frac{{x}^{2}}{2}+(2)\\cdot \\frac{{x}^{3}}{6} \\\\  & =1-x+\\frac{{x}^{3}}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186340398 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "20824866-0419-512a-b241-e3eb66b30194" :knowledge-point/title "Computing the Third-Degree Taylor Polynomial For a Function Given Some Derivatives"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "18e40568-8c1b-55ad-b445-ec0b5bb1110f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4+2(x-7)-3(x-7)^{2}-6(x-7)^{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340400} {:answer/id #uuid "f47222d5-df06-520f-a6d9-af61a4339cfe" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4+2(x-7)-(x-7)^{2}-6(x-7)^{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340401} {:answer/id #uuid "a9e132c0-0d57-55ff-9add-2494b337d488" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4+2(x-7)-2(x-7)^{2}-8(x-7)^{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340402} {:answer/id #uuid "d1f61c9d-4905-50f0-8c64-7c0f6f4c4dc5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4+2(x-7)-3(x-7)^{2}-4(x-7)^{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340403} {:answer/id #uuid "8c8c1bfd-417a-5c0f-b728-254b72d54479" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4+(x-7)-(x-7)^{2}-4(x-7)^{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340404}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d1f61c9d-4905-50f0-8c64-7c0f6f4c4dc5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4+2(x-7)-3(x-7)^{2}-4(x-7)^{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340403} :answer-field/id #uuid "9c59e2e1-832e-53b5-8999-3e4baa093498" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340399}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "bcf4e431-a952-5630-8441-62a79c4f1460" :question/math-academy-id "q-125899" :question/problem "Let $f(x)$ be a function with $f(7)=4,{f}^{′}(7)=2,{f}^{″}(7)=-6$ and ${f}^{‴}(7)=-24.$ Which of the following is the third-degree Taylor polynomial for $f(x)$ about $x=7?$" :question/worked-solution "The third-degree Taylor polynomial of $f(x)$ about $x=7$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{P}_{3}(x) & =f(7)+{f}^{′}(7)(x-7)+\\frac{{f}^{″}(7)}{2!}(x-7)^{2}+\\frac{{f}^{‴}(7)}{3!}(x-7)^{3} \\\\  & =f(7)+{f}^{′}(7)(x-7)+\\frac{{f}^{″}(7)}{2}(x-7)^{2}+\\frac{{f}^{‴}(7)}{6}(x-7)^{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe have been given the following set of values: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(7) & =4 \\\\ {f}^{′}(7) & =2 \\\\ {f}^{″}(7) & =-6 \\\\ {f}^{‴}(7) & =-24.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting the given values into our Taylor polynomial, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{P}_{3}(x) & =4+2(x-7)+\\frac{(-6)}{2}(x-7)^{2}+\\frac{(-24)}{6}(x-7)^{3} \\\\  & =4+2(x-7)-3(x-7)^{2}-4(x-7)^{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186299110 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "5dc0250e-2aa9-5439-b567-93a59fa1c364" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Coefficient of a Term In the Third-Degree Taylor Polynomial of a Given Function"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "edb6346f-f3f4-5495-810e-390a292c326c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{9}{2e}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186299112} {:answer/id #uuid "1ec681c8-3135-5e8a-9397-f90b28ab8d75" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{e}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186299113} {:answer/id #uuid "3c3e88ef-7b25-5185-b4bb-964b09e63769" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{3e}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186299114} {:answer/id #uuid "fef50d72-caab-533d-baf6-ceda9d40b95d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{9e}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186299115} {:answer/id #uuid "ac9c647c-ed20-5cf6-8f3a-c03828dd35a1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{3}{2e}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186299116}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "fef50d72-caab-533d-baf6-ceda9d40b95d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{9e}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186299115} :answer-field/id #uuid "1d563fe2-dd63-5960-a14f-187c6213f838" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186299111}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "08d71aeb-7de0-52ea-9534-27a1ab41e61f" :question/math-academy-id "q-125925" :question/problem "What is the coefficient of ${(x+\\frac{1}{3})}^{3}$ in the third-degree Taylor polynomial of $f(x)={e}^{-3x}$ about $x=-\\frac{1}{3}?$" :question/worked-solution "The coefficient of ${(x+\\frac{1}{3})}^{3}$ is $\\frac{1}{3!}{f}^{(3)}(-\\frac{1}{3}).$ Let's compute the necessary derivatives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x) & ={e}^{-3x} \\\\ {f}^{′}(x) & =-3{e}^{-3x} \\\\ {f}^{″}(x) & =9{e}^{-3x} \\\\ {f}^{‴}(x) & =-27{e}^{-3x}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we evaluate ${f}^{‴}(-\\frac{1}{3}),$ which gives\n\n$$\n{f}^{‴}(-\\frac{1}{3})=-27\\cdot {e}^{-3\\cdot (-1/3)}=-27e.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\frac{1}{3!}{f}^{‴}(-\\frac{1}{3})=\\frac{1}{6}\\cdot (-27e)=-\\frac{9e}{2}.\n$$\n\nSo the coefficient of ${(x+\\frac{1}{3})}^{3}$ is $-\\frac{9e}{2}.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186340405 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "5dc0250e-2aa9-5439-b567-93a59fa1c364" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Coefficient of a Term In the Third-Degree Taylor Polynomial of a Given Function"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4a53711d-af4e-5cce-9fac-361accefdd42" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340407} {:answer/id #uuid "34d30c09-f20e-5c1c-a5af-232ba2e16174" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340408} {:answer/id #uuid "381e07d1-b15c-503d-ab39-f4bcedecd81d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340409} {:answer/id #uuid "a426abc4-a409-5441-8307-9894921ac337" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{48}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340410} {:answer/id #uuid "3c948602-d09f-5030-8b6f-b470b8936046" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{24}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340411}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3c948602-d09f-5030-8b6f-b470b8936046" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{24}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340411} :answer-field/id #uuid "aebd5143-a59e-53a2-af4e-cac6cbdb03da" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340406}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "47beb5c7-b9f8-5cdc-a46a-e7eedfb53a9c" :question/math-academy-id "q-126357" :question/problem "What is the coefficient of ${x}^{3}$ in the third-degree Taylor polynomial of $f(x)=\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2-x)$ about $x=0?$" :question/worked-solution "The coefficient of ${x}^{3}$ is $\\frac{1}{3!}{f}^{(3)}(0).$ Let's compute the necessary derivatives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x) & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2-x) \\\\ {f}^{′}(x) & =-\\frac{1}{2-x} \\\\ {f}^{″}(x) & =-\\frac{1}{(2-x)^{2}} \\\\ {f}^{‴}(x) & =-\\frac{2}{(2-x)^{3}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we evaluate ${f}^{‴}(0),$ which gives\n\n$$\n{f}^{‴}(0)=-\\frac{2}{(2-0)^{3}}=-\\frac{1}{4}.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\frac{1}{3!}{f}^{‴}(0)=\\frac{1}{6}\\cdot (-\\frac{1}{4})=-\\frac{1}{24}.\n$$\n\nSo the coefficient of ${x}^{3}$ is $-\\frac{1}{24}.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186331939 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "5dc0250e-2aa9-5439-b567-93a59fa1c364" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Coefficient of a Term In the Third-Degree Taylor Polynomial of a Given Function"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e28d33c6-9b54-5018-8c30-20b4328565a7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331941} {:answer/id #uuid "f64f7624-f5e2-5746-81d4-517943568d06" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331942} {:answer/id #uuid "377d4d07-1be2-5ae5-a838-0cd5db52bc19" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331943} {:answer/id #uuid "4ab1012d-433c-5c61-b762-c95a6cfddbbd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331944} {:answer/id #uuid "aab72c3b-3e42-516f-81fc-8d253ba110c7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331945}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "377d4d07-1be2-5ae5-a838-0cd5db52bc19" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331943} :answer-field/id #uuid "3cd34680-796d-5b2d-a195-fe32a22dd5ff" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331940}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "384d449f-273e-593f-9d4d-a9fdf55ff2d4" :question/math-academy-id "q-126359" :question/problem "What is the coefficient of ${x}^{3}$ in the third-degree Taylor polynomial of $f(x)=\\frac{1}{1-x}$ about $x=0?$" :question/worked-solution "The coefficient of ${x}^{3}$ is $\\frac{1}{3!}{f}^{(3)}(0).$ Let's compute the necessary derivatives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x) & =\\frac{1}{1-x} \\\\ {f}^{′}(x) & =\\frac{1}{(1-x)^{2}} \\\\ {f}^{″}(x) & =\\frac{2}{(1-x)^{3}} \\\\ {f}^{‴}(x) & =\\frac{6}{(1-x)^{4}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we evaluate ${f}^{‴}(0),$ which gives\n\n$$\n{f}^{‴}(0)=\\frac{6}{(1-0)^{4}}=6.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\frac{1}{3!}{f}^{‴}(0)=\\frac{1}{6}\\cdot 6=1.\n$$\n\nSo the coefficient of ${x}^{3}$ is $1.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186340412 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "5dc0250e-2aa9-5439-b567-93a59fa1c364" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Coefficient of a Term In the Third-Degree Taylor Polynomial of a Given Function"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1e24fd73-3730-544b-b72d-0d2cec8818fc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{24}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340414}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1e24fd73-3730-544b-b72d-0d2cec8818fc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{24}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340414} :answer-field/id #uuid "1714e555-7ad7-52f7-aa9d-1acbe22fde82" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340413}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "56837e97-06d8-5989-94c8-2e9269703dbe" :question/math-academy-id "q-348019" :question/problem "Find the coefficient of ${x}^{3}$ in the third-degree Taylor polynomial of $f(x)=\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2+x)$ about $x=0.$ Do not round the answer.\n\nThe coefficient of ${x}^{3}$ is\n{{field-1}}." :question/worked-solution "The coefficient of ${x}^{3}$ is $\\frac{1}{3!}{f}^{(3)}(0).$ Let's compute the necessary derivatives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x) & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2+x) \\\\ {f}^{′}(x) & =\\frac{1}{2+x} \\\\ {f}^{″}(x) & =-\\frac{1}{(2+x)^{2}} \\\\ {f}^{‴}(x) & =\\frac{2}{(2+x)^{3}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we evaluate ${f}^{‴}(0),$ which gives\n\n$$\n{f}^{‴}(0)=\\frac{2}{(2+0)^{3}}=\\frac{2}{8}=\\frac{1}{4}.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\frac{1}{3!}{f}^{‴}(0)=\\frac{1}{3!}\\cdot \\frac{1}{4}=\\frac{1}{24}.\n$$\n\nSo, the coefficient of ${x}^{3}$ is $\\frac{1}{24}.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186299132 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "f9ea3dac-cf0a-5d05-8d77-7280ce9b5a94" :knowledge-point/title "Computing the Third-Degree Taylor Polynomial For a Given Function About a Given Point"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "82004c40-36ff-54e3-a117-60053abe1ea6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{x^2}{2}+\\frac{x^3}{6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186299134} {:answer/id #uuid "273e0d83-b1bb-517e-8e84-a6659e824e6c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x^2+x^3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186299135}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "82004c40-36ff-54e3-a117-60053abe1ea6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{x^2}{2}+\\frac{x^3}{6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186299134} :answer-field/id #uuid "5026c3a2-d7a9-5597-b05d-fb76a330690c" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186299133}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "59c53cd6-fa80-5ad8-96c0-683e85a578cf" :question/math-academy-id "q-348351" :question/problem "Find the third-degree Taylor polynomial ${P}_{3}(x)$ of $f(x)={e}^{x}$ about $x=0.$\n\n${P}_{3}(x)=1+x\\,+$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "To find the third-degree Taylor polynomial about $x=0,$ we plug $a=0$ into the general formula to give\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{P}_{3}(x) & =f(0)+{f}^{′}(0)x+{f}^{″}(0)\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2!}+{f}^{‴}(0)\\frac{{x}^{3}}{3!} \\\\  & =f(0)+{f}^{′}(0)x+{f}^{″}(0)\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2}+{f}^{‴}(0)\\frac{{x}^{3}}{6}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe need to compute $f(0),$ ${f}^{′}(0),$ ${f}^{″}(0),$ and ${f}^{‴}(0),$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x) & ={e}^{x} & ⟹ &  & f(0) & ={e}^{0}=1 \\\\ {f}^{′}(x) & ={e}^{x} & ⟹ &  & {f}^{′}(0) & ={e}^{0}=1 \\\\ {f}^{″}(x) & ={e}^{x} & ⟹ &  & {f}^{″}(0) & ={e}^{0}=1 \\\\ {f}^{‴}(x) & ={e}^{x} & ⟹ &  & {f}^{‴}(0) & ={e}^{0}=1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we plug the results for $f(0),$ ${f}^{′}(0),$ ${f}^{″}(0),$ and ${f}^{‴}(0)$ into our third-degree Taylor polynomial. This gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{P}_{3}(x) & =1+1\\cdot x+1\\cdot \\frac{{x}^{2}}{2}+1\\cdot \\frac{{x}^{3}}{6} \\\\  & =1+x+\\frac{1}{2}{x}^{2}+\\frac{1}{6}{x}^{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186299140 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "20824866-0419-512a-b241-e3eb66b30194" :knowledge-point/title "Computing the Third-Degree Taylor Polynomial For a Function Given Some Derivatives"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "472c1f6c-c426-57a7-8cdf-7bafca8df524" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186299142} {:answer/id #uuid "4c1088db-22d5-54b6-a598-f210b1474a68" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340415}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "472c1f6c-c426-57a7-8cdf-7bafca8df524" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186299142} :answer-field/id #uuid "b7eb20cc-60b3-5716-8615-7096d3484a2a" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186299141} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "bf422be2-b937-5580-a34e-02332b04a06e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186299144}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "bf422be2-b937-5580-a34e-02332b04a06e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186299144} :answer-field/id #uuid "f43eea49-5861-5c23-a4e7-599126acb8b0" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186299143} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "47b9e4f9-3613-5f6e-ab98-5e24149dc18b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186299146}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "47b9e4f9-3613-5f6e-ab98-5e24149dc18b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186299146} :answer-field/id #uuid "0826953c-095a-5c6e-961b-c6d6d80a8ce3" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186299145}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "73fdece9-8d01-59ea-89e6-8519efac60d3" :question/math-academy-id "q-351832" :question/problem "Let $f(x)$ be a function with $f(2)=5,{f}^{′}(2)=3,{f}^{″}(2)=4,$ and ${f}^{‴}(2)=-6.$ What is the third-degree Taylor polynomial ${P}_{3}(x)$ for $f(x)$ about $x=2?$\n\n${P}_{3}(x)=5\\,+$\n{{field-1}}\n$(x-2)\\,+$\n{{field-2}}\n$(x-2)^{2}\\,-$\n{{field-3}}\n$(x-2)^{3}$" :question/worked-solution "The third-degree Taylor polynomial of $f(x)$ about $x=2$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{P}_{3}(x) & =f(2)+{f}^{′}(2)(x-2)+\\frac{{f}^{″}(2)}{2!}(x-2)^{2}+\\frac{{f}^{‴}(2)}{3!}(x-2)^{3} \\\\  & =f(2)+{f}^{′}(2)(x-2)+\\frac{{f}^{″}(2)}{2}(x-2)^{2}+\\frac{{f}^{‴}(2)}{6}(x-2)^{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe have been given the following set of values: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(2) & =5 \\\\ {f}^{′}(2) & =3 \\\\ {f}^{″}(2) & =4 \\\\ {f}^{‴}(2) & =-6\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting the given values into our Taylor polynomial, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{P}_{3}(x) & =5+(3)\\cdot (x-2)+\\frac{4}{2}\\cdot (x-2)^{2}+\\frac{(-6)}{6}\\cdot (x-2)^{3} \\\\  & =5+3\\,(x-2)+2\\,(x-2)^{2}-1\\,(x-2)^{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186331953 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "f9ea3dac-cf0a-5d05-8d77-7280ce9b5a94" :knowledge-point/title "Computing the Third-Degree Taylor Polynomial For a Given Function About a Given Point"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3ba2eba6-98da-551a-a9d7-eaba0126d0c6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2x^2-\\frac{4}{3}x^3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331955}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3ba2eba6-98da-551a-a9d7-eaba0126d0c6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2x^2-\\frac{4}{3}x^3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331955} :answer-field/id #uuid "f2a61a26-d697-50e5-9a14-f09ca5b0e334" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331954}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "783fb36c-345a-5c94-9d91-f565c09ac763" :question/math-academy-id "q-351859" :question/problem "Find the third-degree Taylor polynomial ${P}_{3}(x)$ of $f(x)={e}^{-2x}$ about $x=0.$\n\n${P}_{3}(x)=1-2x\\,+$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "To find the third-degree Taylor polynomial about $x=0,$ we plug $a=0$ into the general formula to give\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{P}_{3}(x) & =f(0)+{f}^{′}(0)x+{f}^{″}(0)\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2!}+{f}^{‴}(0)\\frac{{x}^{3}}{3!} \\\\  & =f(0)+{f}^{′}(0)x+{f}^{″}(0)\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2}+{f}^{‴}(0)\\frac{{x}^{3}}{6}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe need to compute $f(0),$ ${f}^{′}(0),$ ${f}^{″}(0),$ and ${f}^{‴}(0),$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x) & ={e}^{-2x} & ⟹ &  & f(0) & ={e}^{-0}=1 \\\\ {f}^{′}(x) & =-2{e}^{-2x} & ⟹ &  & {f}^{′}(0) & =-2{e}^{-0}=-2 \\\\ {f}^{″}(x) & =4{e}^{-2x} & ⟹ &  & {f}^{″}(0) & =4{e}^{-0}=4 \\\\ {f}^{‴}(x) & =-8{e}^{-2x} & ⟹ &  & {f}^{‴}(0) & =-8{e}^{-0}=-8\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we plug the results for $f(0),$ ${f}^{′}(0),$ ${f}^{″}(0),$ and ${f}^{‴}(0)$ into our third-degree Taylor polynomial. This gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{P}_{3}(x) & =1-2\\cdot x+4\\cdot \\frac{{x}^{2}}{2}-8\\cdot \\frac{{x}^{3}}{6} \\\\  & =1-2x+2{x}^{2}-\\frac{4}{3}{x}^{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186340416 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "5dc0250e-2aa9-5439-b567-93a59fa1c364" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Coefficient of a Term In the Third-Degree Taylor Polynomial of a Given Function"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "038d5daa-95f1-5dbb-971a-a26686b08e71" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{81}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340418} {:answer/id #uuid "de62eb2c-63f6-5372-a9ca-53858179ecf4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{81}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340419}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "038d5daa-95f1-5dbb-971a-a26686b08e71" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{81}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340418} :answer-field/id #uuid "e027e265-2e46-5698-a52e-62df8c16cb38" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340417}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "962c443b-40cc-5a79-88ee-071a8061f1eb" :question/math-academy-id "q-351869" :question/problem "Find the coefficient of $(x-3)^{3}$ in the third-degree Taylor polynomial of $f(x)=\\frac{1}{x}$ about $x=3.$ Do not round the answer.\n\nThe coefficient of $(x-3)^{3}$ is\n{{field-1}}." :question/worked-solution "The coefficient of $(x-3)^{3}$ is $\\frac{1}{3!}{f}^{‴}(3).$ Let's compute the necessary derivatives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x) & =\\frac{1}{x} \\\\ {f}^{′}(x) & =-\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}} \\\\ {f}^{″}(x) & =\\frac{2}{{x}^{3}} \\\\ {f}^{‴}(x) & =-\\frac{6}{{x}^{4}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we evaluate ${f}^{‴}(3),$ which gives\n\n$$\n{f}^{‴}(3)=-\\frac{6}{{3}^{4}}=-\\frac{6}{81}=-\\frac{2}{27}.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\frac{1}{3!}{f}^{‴}(3)=\\frac{1}{3!}\\cdot (-\\frac{2}{27})=-\\frac{2}{6\\cdot 27}=-\\frac{1}{81}.\n$$\n\nSo, the coefficient of $(x-3)^{3}$ is $-\\frac{1}{81}.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186299157 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "f9ea3dac-cf0a-5d05-8d77-7280ce9b5a94" :knowledge-point/title "Computing the Third-Degree Taylor Polynomial For a Given Function About a Given Point"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "cf6e9030-57c3-59fa-81ce-a8b7835a0a39" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2e^2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186299159}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "cf6e9030-57c3-59fa-81ce-a8b7835a0a39" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2e^2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186299159} :answer-field/id #uuid "3562a69b-e327-5620-83fb-6a373ebf3022" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186299158} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "de644758-994f-55fe-abc6-49e72af9457b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2e^2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186299161}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "de644758-994f-55fe-abc6-49e72af9457b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2e^2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186299161} :answer-field/id #uuid "2420db8b-134f-5d2a-9dc0-2dfb5c64d28e" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186299160} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ee96f042-d14a-5dc4-80e1-8caff2f3963d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{4e^2}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186299163}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ee96f042-d14a-5dc4-80e1-8caff2f3963d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{4e^2}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186299163} :answer-field/id #uuid "bb205273-e4b9-50f1-9d87-6f2fcbdf52a7" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186299162}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "1131e7ab-49a4-5f65-ba00-78426956eaa5" :question/math-academy-id "q-351997" :question/problem "Find the third-degree Taylor polynomial ${P}_{3}(x)$ of $f(x)={e}^{2x}$ about $x=1.$ Do not round the answer.\n\n${P}_{3}(x)={e}^{2}\\,+$\n{{field-1}}\n$(x-1)\\,+$\n{{field-2}}\n$(x-1)^{2}\\,+$\n{{field-3}}\n$(x-1)^{3}$" :question/worked-solution "To find the third-degree Taylor polynomial about $x=1,$ we plug $a=1$ into the general formula to give \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{P}_{3}(x)=f(1)+{f}^{′}(1)(x-1)+\\frac{{f}^{″}(1)}{2!}(x-1)^{2}+\\frac{{f}^{‴}(1)}{3!}(x-1)^{3} \\\\ {P}_{3}(x)=f(1)+{f}^{′}(1)(x-1)+\\frac{{f}^{″}(1)}{2}(x-1)^{2}+\\frac{{f}^{‴}(1)}{6}(x-1)^{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe need to compute $f(1),$ ${f}^{′}(1),$ ${f}^{″}(1),$ and ${f}^{‴}(1),$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x) & ={e}^{2x} & ⟹ &  & f(1) & ={e}^{2\\cdot 1}={e}^{2} \\\\ {f}^{′}(x) & =2{e}^{2x} & ⟹ &  & {f}^{′}(1) & =2{e}^{2\\cdot 1}=2{e}^{2} \\\\ {f}^{″}(x) & =4{e}^{2x} & ⟹ &  & {f}^{″}(1) & =4{e}^{2\\cdot 1}=4{e}^{2} \\\\ {f}^{‴}(x) & =8{e}^{2x} & ⟹ &  & {f}^{‴}(1) & =8{e}^{2\\cdot 1}=8{e}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we plug the results for $f(1),$ ${f}^{′}(1),$ ${f}^{″}(1),$ and ${f}^{‴}(1)$ into our third-degree Taylor polynomial. This gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{P}_{3}(x)={e}^{2}+2{e}^{2}(x-1)+2{e}^{2}(x-1)^{2}+\\frac{4{e}^{2}}{3}(x-1)^{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186340420 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "f9ea3dac-cf0a-5d05-8d77-7280ce9b5a94" :knowledge-point/title "Computing the Third-Degree Taylor Polynomial For a Given Function About a Given Point"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "89e4e2d3-bb9f-5cb0-9912-cb22108c54cb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340422} {:answer/id #uuid "6235f995-c6c0-5765-9ecb-88f0d8f6085c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340423}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "89e4e2d3-bb9f-5cb0-9912-cb22108c54cb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340422} :answer-field/id #uuid "eb3d9fdb-6377-5367-b531-9d53d7688c03" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340421} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "43ec6938-737c-5a65-a523-a1c5bdbad0be" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340425}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "43ec6938-737c-5a65-a523-a1c5bdbad0be" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340425} :answer-field/id #uuid "9a9a0e41-73e9-5db4-878c-0999e46ae436" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340424} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9281c7e1-0281-556b-987b-54a366fc4e3a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340427}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9281c7e1-0281-556b-987b-54a366fc4e3a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340427} :answer-field/id #uuid "2848f22c-fc19-56af-985a-1ab54c1d6592" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340426}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "d447ff59-5163-5274-8987-8699bd1198dd" :question/math-academy-id "q-351999" :question/problem "Find the third-degree Taylor polynomial ${P}_{3}(x)$ of $f(x)=\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}}$ about $x=1.$ Do not round the answer.\n\n${P}_{3}(x)=1\\,-$\n{{field-1}}\n$(x-1)\\,+$\n{{field-2}}\n$(x-1)^{2}\\,-$\n{{field-3}}\n$(x-1)^{3}$" :question/worked-solution "To find the third-degree Taylor polynomial about $x=1,$ we plug $a=1$ into the general formula to give \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{P}_{3}(x)=f(1)+{f}^{′}(1)(x-1)+\\frac{{f}^{″}(1)}{2!}(x-1)^{2}+\\frac{{f}^{‴}(1)}{3!}(x-1)^{3} \\\\ {P}_{3}(x)=f(1)+{f}^{′}(1)(x-1)+\\frac{{f}^{″}(1)}{2}(x-1)^{2}+\\frac{{f}^{‴}(1)}{6}(x-1)^{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe need to compute $f(1),$ ${f}^{′}(1),$ ${f}^{″}(1),$ and ${f}^{‴}(1),$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x) & =\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}} & ⟹ &  & f(1) & =\\frac{1}{{1}^{2}}=1 \\\\ {f}^{′}(x) & =-\\frac{2}{{x}^{3}} & ⟹ &  & {f}^{′}(1) & =-\\frac{2}{{1}^{3}}=-2 \\\\ {f}^{″}(x) & =\\frac{6}{{x}^{4}} & ⟹ &  & {f}^{″}(1) & =\\frac{6}{{1}^{4}}=6 \\\\ {f}^{‴}(x) & =-\\frac{24}{{x}^{5}} & ⟹ &  & {f}^{‴}(1) & =-\\frac{24}{{1}^{5}}=-24\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we plug the results for $f(1),$ ${f}^{′}(1),$ ${f}^{″}(1),$ and ${f}^{‴}(1)$ into our third-degree Taylor polynomial. This gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{P}_{3}(x) & =(1)+(-2)\\cdot (x-1)+\\frac{(6)}{2}\\cdot (x-1)^{2}+\\frac{(-24)}{6}\\cdot (x-1)^{3} \\\\  & =1-2(x-1)+3(x-1)^{2}-4(x-1)^{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186101384 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "20824866-0419-512a-b241-e3eb66b30194" :knowledge-point/title "Computing the Third-Degree Taylor Polynomial For a Function Given Some Derivatives"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "84caa4ca-c232-5208-be43-a92090431d47" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1 - (x + 4) - 2(x + 4)^{2} + 2(x + 4)^{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186099901} {:answer/id #uuid "bbf892fa-5884-52d9-8c6f-ec9c4e1e0d7d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1 - (x - 4) - 2(x - 4)^{2} + 12(x - 4)^{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186099902} {:answer/id #uuid "c18da08c-7de5-5ede-8888-76eb1b1ca737" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1 - (x - 4) - (x - 4)^{2} + 2(x - 4)^{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186099903} {:answer/id #uuid "07ea8d3e-c124-5a45-ad14-b59ed2aaea94" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1 - (x - 4) - (x - 4)^{2} + (x - 4)^{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186099904} {:answer/id #uuid "75930186-551a-54f6-8919-da2afb95a78d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1 - (x + 4) - 2(x + 4)^{2} + 12(x + 4)^{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186099905}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c18da08c-7de5-5ede-8888-76eb1b1ca737" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1 - (x - 4) - (x - 4)^{2} + 2(x - 4)^{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186099903} :answer-field/id #uuid "ee633f70-d71c-56c8-825f-ae5bc5715654" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186099900}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "31b1226d-bfa8-57f5-ba65-3595a00fc98e" :question/math-academy-id "q-51235" :question/problem "Let $f(x)$ be a function with $f(4)=1,{f}^{′}(4)=-1,{f}^{″}(4)=-2$ and ${f}^{‴}(4)=12.$ Which of the following is the third-degree Taylor polynomial for $f(x)$ about $x=4?$" :question/worked-solution "The third-degree Taylor polynomial of $f(x)$ about $x=4$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{P}_{3}(x) & =f(4)+{f}^{′}(4)(x-4)+\\frac{{f}^{″}(4)}{2!}(x-4)^{2}+\\frac{{f}^{‴}(4)}{3!}(x-4)^{3} \\\\  & =f(4)+{f}^{′}(4)(x-4)+\\frac{{f}^{″}(4)}{2}(x-4)^{2}+\\frac{{f}^{‴}(4)}{6}(x-4)^{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe have been given the following set of values: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(4) & =1 \\\\ {f}^{′}(4) & =-1 \\\\ {f}^{″}(4) & =-2 \\\\ {f}^{‴}(4) & =12.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting the given values into our Taylor polynomial, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{P}_{3}(x) & =1-1(x-4)+\\frac{(-2)}{2}(x-4)^{2}+\\frac{12}{6}(x-4)^{3} \\\\  & =1-(x-4)-(x-4)^{2}+2(x-4)^{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186340428 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "20824866-0419-512a-b241-e3eb66b30194" :knowledge-point/title "Computing the Third-Degree Taylor Polynomial For a Function Given Some Derivatives"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "52ba7736-d88d-59ad-b210-ee6a42195079" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3+5(x+2)-8(x+2)^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340430} {:answer/id #uuid "7dd47933-e029-596c-8e31-b5e501eff97a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3+5(x-2)-8(x-2)^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340431} {:answer/id #uuid "cdedd75a-3353-55da-9ea9-8dc15556a102" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3+5(x+2)-(x+2)^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340432} {:answer/id #uuid "5670c9ff-0f62-58e2-a98c-89f91fa83663" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3+5(x+2)-4(x+2)^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340433} {:answer/id #uuid "af97abf0-0855-5889-9608-6c7b091961d9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3+5(x-2)-(x-2)^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340434}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5670c9ff-0f62-58e2-a98c-89f91fa83663" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3+5(x+2)-4(x+2)^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340433} :answer-field/id #uuid "f0fe6001-0c14-5d20-9880-f98f67d3f814" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340429}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "35ff3098-4ddf-599c-bbdc-f3a31be635b8" :question/math-academy-id "q-51237" :question/problem "Let $f$ be a function with $f(-2)=3,{f}^{′}(-2)=5,{f}^{″}(-2)=-8$ and ${f}^{‴}(-2)=0.$ Which of the following is the third-degree Taylor polynomial for $f$ about $x=-2?$" :question/worked-solution "The third-degree Taylor polynomial of $f(x)$ about $x=-2$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{P}_{3}(x) & =f(-2)+{f}^{′}(-2)(x+2)+\\frac{{f}^{″}(-2)}{2!}(x+2)^{2}+\\frac{{f}^{‴}(-2)}{3!}(x+2)^{3} \\\\  & =f(-2)+{f}^{′}(-2)(x+2)+\\frac{{f}^{″}(2)}{2}(x+2)^{2}+\\frac{{f}^{‴}(-2)}{6}(x+2)^{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe have been given the following set of values: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(-2) & =3 \\\\ {f}^{′}(-2) & =5 \\\\ {f}^{″}(-2) & =-8 \\\\ {f}^{‴}(-2) & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting the given values into our Taylor polynomial, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{P}_{3}(x) & =3+5(x+2)+\\frac{-8}{2}(x+2)^{2}+\\frac{0}{6}(x+2)^{3} \\\\  & =3+5(x+2)-4(x+2)^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186299164 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "20824866-0419-512a-b241-e3eb66b30194" :knowledge-point/title "Computing the Third-Degree Taylor Polynomial For a Function Given Some Derivatives"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f926d18b-bece-552a-b462-9bfdb138245e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1+(x-3)+2(x-3)^{2}+\\frac{1}{2}(x-3)^{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186299166} {:answer/id #uuid "6bd88972-4780-5d92-a543-49b58906671b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1+(x-3)+(x-3)^{2}+3(x-3)^{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186299167} {:answer/id #uuid "66543ae0-9635-578f-86c6-5e9b5bd97746" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1+(x-3)+2(x-3)^{2}+3(x-3)^{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186299168} {:answer/id #uuid "a52b8ad2-06c5-52a6-81e5-95eeba5e4c80" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1+(x-3)+(x-3)^{2}+\\frac{1}{2}(x-3)^{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186299169} {:answer/id #uuid "df9b5959-3d38-5cad-b03e-665e73cc3f07" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1+(x-3)+(x-3)^{2}+\\frac{1}{3}(x-3)^{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186299170}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a52b8ad2-06c5-52a6-81e5-95eeba5e4c80" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1+(x-3)+(x-3)^{2}+\\frac{1}{2}(x-3)^{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186299169} :answer-field/id #uuid "d5e5319b-db58-59d1-9451-cf5857ebe2e5" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186299165}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "ceac79ef-722b-5480-8037-3bc64c4e23ab" :question/math-academy-id "q-51238" :question/problem "Let $f$ be a function with $f(3)=1,{f}^{′}(3)=1,{f}^{″}(3)=2$ and ${f}^{‴}(3)=3.$ Which of the following is the third-degree Taylor polynomial for $f$ about $x=3?$" :question/worked-solution "The third-degree Taylor polynomial of $f(x)$ about $x=3$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{P}_{3}(x) & =f(3)+{f}^{′}(3)(x-3)+\\frac{{f}^{″}(3)}{2!}(x-3)^{2}+\\frac{{f}^{‴}(3)}{3!}(x-3)^{3} \\\\  & =f(3)+{f}^{′}(3)(x-3)+\\frac{{f}^{″}(3)}{2}(x-3)^{2}+\\frac{{f}^{‴}(3)}{6}(x-3)^{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe have been given the following set of values: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(3) & =1 \\\\ {f}^{′}(3) & =1 \\\\ {f}^{″}(3) & =2 \\\\ {f}^{‴}(3) & =3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting the given values into our Taylor polynomial, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{P}_{3}(x) & =1+1(x-3)+\\frac{2}{2}(x-3)^{2}+\\frac{3}{6}(x-3)^{3} \\\\  & =1+(x-3)+(x-3)^{2}+\\frac{1}{2}(x-3)^{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}]}
